\title{noisecanceling: Correcting Questionnaires for Acquiescence Response Bias}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Tools for measuring and correcting acquiescence response bias (the tendency to agree with items regardless of their content) in psychological questionnaires built with balanced scales. Balanced scales pair positively keyed (PK) and negatively keyed (NK) items so that a per-person acquiescence index can be estimated and removed by centering item responses. The approach works like noise-cancelling headphones: the trait is the signal, acquiescence is the noise, and inverting the negatively keyed items aligns the signal so that the noise cancels out. The package implements the classical centering correction together with helpers for scoring, classical psychometric analysis, and reporting.
}
